From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 05:57:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: drop wifi config call from ieee80211 hotplug

The ieee80211 hotplug ran 'wifi config' concurrently with the boot-time
uci-defaults scripts writing the wireless config. uci batch is not
atomic and its commit truncates the shared delta file, so concurrent
writers corrupt /etc/config/wireless: radio sections land mid-file and
uncommitted options are silently lost.

The call only ever wrote on factory and post-sysupgrade first boots,
exactly when the defaults scripts run; the defaults sequence now
generates the radio sections itself. On all other boots the radios
already exist in the config and the call was a no-op. Keep the
network.wireless retry so netifd picks up phys that register after its
config load.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect
+++ b/src/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/10-wifi-detect
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #!/bin/sh
 
+# wireless config generation happens in the uci-defaults sequence;
+# running 'wifi config' here raced those scripts' uncommitted changes
 [ "${ACTION}" = "add" ] && {
-	/sbin/wifi config
 	ubus call network.wireless retry
 }
